{%- comment -%}
  Screens: cancellation flow (1 choose subscription → 2 before you cancel →
  3 why you started → 4 facts & alternatives → 5 cancellation reason →
  6 adjust your routine → 7 40% off next delivery → 8 confirm →
  9 cancelled), reactivation, inactive list, empty account.

  Step 7 (cancel-savings) is the ONE place the 40% offer is ever shown, for
  every reason the backend marks eligible (retentionOfferRedeemed false) —
  not just "Too expensive" as before. Step 6 (cancel-offer, "Adjust your
  routine") keeps its reason-personalized recommendation but no longer
  shows the offer itself, so it appears exactly once in the journey. A
  customer who already redeemed it skips step 7 only — show() redirects
  straight to cancel-confirm — and still reaches Final Confirmation.

  Ported from the approved Claude Design mockup ("VetPets Portal V2"),
  which frames step 1 as choosing WHICH SUBSCRIPTION to cancel, on the
  premise that every product is its own subscription. Phoenix has no such
  thing: one subscription, holding one or more product lines, and
  cancel(id) always ends the whole thing — there is no per-line cancel.
  See cancel-choose below for how that is reconciled, and cancel-confirm /
  cancelFacts in subscription-portal.js for where it matters most: the
  screen the customer commits on must never suggest that only one product
  is affected.

  Where a real subscription holds exactly one product, that product is
  named directly on the started/reason/retention screens (see
  cancel.focusName / cancel.reasonHeading / cancel.startedHeading in
  viewModel()) — the vast majority of accounts. A multi-product
  subscription falls back to generic "Routine Care" wording on those same
  screens, because there is no honest way to speak for the whole
  subscription in the name of just one of its products.

  Cancellation stays completable throughout: the save-offers are shown
  once, and "continue cancellation" is always present.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- 1 · Choose subscription ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Always renders, even for the single-subscription majority — this is the
  screen the founder asked not to skip. It is deliberately NOT a picker:
  there is one real subscription, shown as one card (pre-selected, and the
  only option), listing every product inside it. Nothing here implies a
  product could be selected and cancelled on its own; the subtitle says so
  outright, replacing the design's own subtitle ("Each product in your
  routine is its own subscription"), which is not true of this data model.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-choose" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cc0-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="subscription">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Subscription
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-cc0-h">Which subscription do you want to cancel?</h1>
    <p class="spp__lede">
      This is the subscription tied to your account. Everything in it is reviewed
      together on the screens that follow.
    </p>

    <div class="spp__choices" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Your subscription">
      <div class="spp__choice spp__choice--stacked spp__choice--sub" role="radio" aria-checked="true" aria-disabled="true">
        <span class="spp__radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="spp__choice-text">
          <b>Routine Care subscription</b>
          <span>
            Every <span data-spp-field="subscription.intervalDays">60</span> days ·
            next <span data-spp-field="subscription.nextOrderShort">Sep 8</span>
          </span>
          <span class="spp__choice-products" data-spp-list="lineThumbs2">
            <template data-spp-tpl="lineThumbs2">
              <span class="spp__thumb spp__thumb--sm" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></span>
            </template>
          </span>
          <span class="spp__choice-summary" data-spp-field="subscription.quantitySummary">FreshWipes ×2, EyeWipes ×1</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:18px;" data-spp-go="cancel-benefits">Continue</button>
    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="subscription">Never mind, take me back</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 2 · Before you cancel ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Rebuilt field-for-field against the approved Claude Design mockup
  ("VetPets Portal V2", the isCancelProof screen) — wide 960px column
  (not this file's usual .spp__narrow), a Back link that returns to step
  1 rather than jumping out of the flow, and the step indicator the
  design itself renders ("Before you cancel · Step 2 of 7" — the design
  counts its own 7 cancel-flow decision screens, with "Cancelled" as the
  terminal outcome afterward, matching this file's 8-screen count).
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-benefits" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cb-h">
  <div class="spp__cancel-wide">
    <div class="spp__step-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="cancel-choose">
        {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Back
      </button>
      <span class="spp__cancel-step">Before you cancel &middot; Step 2 of 8</span>
    </div>

    <div class="spp__cancel-important">
      <div class="spp__cancel-important-head">
        {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'clock-action', size: 20 %}
        <span>Important: before you cancel</span>
      </div>
      <p class="spp__cancel-important-lead">
        <b>95%</b> of VetPets customers see meaningful results after <b>90 days</b> of
        consistent daily use.
      </p>
      <p class="spp__cancel-important-body">
        Daily care takes consistency, and your dog may also need time to become
        comfortable with the routine &mdash; giving it the full 90 days gives both the
        product and your pet a fair chance.
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      "4.8/5 · Trusted by 45,000+ Dog Owners" — the same real, already-
      approved aggregate rating used on the EyeWipes/FreshWipes offer and
      prelander pages. Kept alongside the two real review cards below
      rather than replaced by them: one is the aggregate trust signal,
      the other is specific, attributable proof — the design's own
      review carousel plus this codebase's existing rating row are not
      mutually exclusive.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__trustbar">
      <span class="spp__trustbar-stars" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
      <span>4.8/5 &middot; Trusted by 45,000+ Dog Owners</span>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Two real, verified customer reviews — reproduces the design's own
      review carousel, which its source comments describe as "genuine
      reviews lifted verbatim from the live VetPets homepage reviews
      module." That design picks by a single hardcoded mock product;
      cancelReviews (see listData() in subscription-portal.js) generalizes
      the same idea to whichever real product categories are actually in
      THIS subscription, falling back to a second real quote for the same
      product rather than ever inventing a review for a product the
      customer does not have.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__reviews-panel">
      <div class="spp__reviews-head">What VetPets pet parents are saying</div>
      <div class="spp__reviews-grid" data-spp-list="cancelReviews">
        <template data-spp-tpl="cancelReviews">
          <div class="spp__review-card">
            <div class="spp__review-stars" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>
            <p class="spp__review-quote" data-spp-field="quote"></p>
            <div class="spp__review-meta">
              <span class="spp__review-tag" data-spp-field="category"></span>
              <span class="spp__review-name" data-spp-field="name"></span>
              <span class="spp__review-verified">
                {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'check-circle', size: 12 %}Verified
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </template>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Final veterinarian video — exactly ONE file loaded and shown at a
      time, chosen in JS (see Portal.prototype.syncVetVideo in
      subscription-portal.js), never via the browser's own <source media>
      selection: that mechanism let both the desktop 16:9 file and the
      mobile 1:1 file end up loaded on real devices, so the two videos
      visually overlapped. A single <video> with no <source> children
      and a plain `src` set by JS from the two data-spp-vet-src-* URLs
      below cannot have that failure mode: there is only ever one src.

      No static `poster` attribute here either, for the same reason as
      before: subscription-portal.js loads with `defer` (see
      layout/subscription-portal.liquid), which runs after the HTML
      parses but is not instant, so a hardcoded default would paint the
      wrong viewport's shape first. The gap shows the neutral background
      colour on .spp__vet-video instead, until syncVetVideo sets the real
      matching poster from the two data-spp-vet-poster-* URLs below — each
      one the corresponding file's own real first frame (the veterinarian,
      never the dog-benefits graphic used elsewhere on this screen).

      No autoplay, on either viewport: the video only ever plays from the
      customer's own tap on the custom .spp__vet-video-play button drawn
      over the poster (see syncVetVideo and bindVetVideoControls in
      subscription-portal.js) — that tap is also the user gesture that
      lets JS turn sound on, which a page-initiated autoplay could not do
      reliably. Native `controls` is added only once playback has actually
      started (again in JS), so the un-played poster state shows nothing
      but the custom button — no native scrubber sitting on top of a
      frozen frame.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__eyebrow" style="margin-top:18px;">Watch &middot; about 90 seconds</div>
    <h2 class="spp__h2" style="margin-top:4px;">Why consistency matters</h2>
    <p class="spp__lede spp__cancel-video-lede">
      A short explanation of what daily care is quietly doing for your dog, and what
      changes when it stops.
    </p>
    <div class="spp__vet-video" style="margin-top:10px;">
      <video
        class="spp__vet-video-el"
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        data-spp-vet-src-desktop="https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/be6c0d1c00b3463797270f2fc43c2815.mp4"
        data-spp-vet-src-mobile="https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/1d4391c64d264e46b877c356e1396f4a.mp4"
        data-spp-vet-poster-desktop="{{ 'spp-cancel-benefits-desktop.jpg' | asset_url }}"
        data-spp-vet-poster-mobile="{{ 'spp-cancel-benefits-mobile.jpg' | asset_url }}"
        aria-label="A veterinarian explains why consistency matters for your dog's daily care routine">
      </video>
      <button type="button" class="spp__vet-video-play" aria-label="Play video">
        {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'play', size: 28 %}
      </button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Veterinarian identity/credential card — the same real, already-
      approved "Dr. Michael Thompson, Veterinarian · VetPets" identity
      used on the EyeWipes/FreshWipes offer and prelander pages, not a
      new persona invented for this screen.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__vet-card">
      <img
        class="spp__vet-card-photo"
        src="{{ 'ewof-vet-dr-michael-thompson.webp' | asset_url }}"
        alt="Dr. Michael Thompson" width="48" height="48" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <span class="spp__vet-card-body">
        <b>Dr. Michael Thompson</b>
        <span>Veterinarian &middot; VetPets</span>
      </span>
      <span class="spp__vet-card-badge">
        {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'check-circle', size: 12 %}
        <span>Vet reviewed</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="spp__cancel-cta">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" data-spp-go="subscription">Never mind, keep my Routine Care</button>
      <div class="spp__quiet-row">
        <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="cancel-started">Continue cancellation</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

